efinitely want to keep both Groban and Evans, and haven&#39;t heard any reason not to retain the others</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R16" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>17</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2"></td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R17" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>18</div></th><td class="s0" colspan="2">School</td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2"></td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R18" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>19</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/superintendent-of-public-instruction/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976469797&amp;usg=AOvVaw139kjEhGKBczUhYK-DXZo2">State Superintendent</a></td><td class="s1">Richard Barrera</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Barerra is the only Democratic candidate</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R19" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>20</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2"></td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R20" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>21</div></th><td class="s0" colspan="2">Propositions</td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2"></td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R21" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>22</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-1-housing-bond/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976470148&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_vq5ExCsDU9qUZKDMqUmo">Prop 1 - Housing bond</a></td><td class="s1">✅✅</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">More affordable housing is needed now and funding for it is the main blocker</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R22" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>23</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-2-rainy-day-fund/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976470329&amp;usg=AOvVaw0F-gq3RpxKI7JV-WJVVAeJ">Prop 2 - Rainy day fund</a></td><td class="s1">✅✅</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">We should remove the Gann Limit completely, but this at least allows CA to save more during boom times</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R23" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>24</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-3-high-income-tax/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976470661&amp;usg=AOvVaw1asvdurb_SjCeKoz_f5zDc">Prop 3 - High-income tax</a></td><td class="s1">✅✅</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Schools need money more than people who collect $360k+</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R24" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>25</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-4-public-fundraising/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976470792&amp;usg=AOvVaw21LGogDXf--etd4AtlD-TY">Prop 4 - Public fundraising</a></td><td class="s1">✅</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Cities should be allowed to publically finance candidates as some check on the excesses of corporate lobbying</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R25" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>26</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-5-recall-reform/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976470907&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ao6X_wFePqUPsBQQbjggU">Prop 5 - Recall reform</a></td><td class="s1">✅</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">More reform for recalls are needed to ensure that cannot be used undemocratically, this is a small start</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R26" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>27</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-37-homebuyers-loan/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976471045&amp;usg=AOvVaw2zApZC6y04HWRVgyh7yl8S">Prop 37 - Homebuyers loan</a></td><td class="s1">❌</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Don&#39;t bid up the price of housing without fixing the real problem which is lack of affordable supply</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R27" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>28</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-38-research-bond/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976471181&amp;usg=AOvVaw14ddTP-9npJ-IzGNDBhFo0">Prop 38 - Research bond</a></td><td class="s1">❌</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">More research funding is good, but don&#39;t dedicate funding to a specific institution</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R28" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>29</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-39-voter-id/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976471420&amp;usg=AOvVaw1YNptT78QWwuW6LZCeZG7b">Prop 39 - Voter ID</a></td><td class="s1">❌❌</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Voter ID doesn&#39;t solve any problems and just introduces lots of new ones for no reason</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R29" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>30</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-40-billionaire-tax/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976471688&amp;usg=AOvVaw0d0aVwPHP8SXw1TVD0k77T">Prop 40 - Billionaire tax</a></td><td class="s1">✅✅✅</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Small tax that billionaires won&#39;t even notice builds momentum for a permanent nationwide tax like Norway, and saves healthcare for millions!</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R30" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>31</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-41-tax-audits/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976471894&amp;usg=AOvVaw28H0ozADbXFZdhHDj7WoFn">Prop 41 - Spending limits</a></td><td class="s1">❌❌❌</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Don&#39;t let billionaires buy themselves an exemption to paying taxes!</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R31" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>32</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-42-property-taxes/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976472101&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QjcjZfuc3pZ0MjNttHckl">Prop 42 - Ban asset taxes</a></td><td class="s1">❌❌❌</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Don&#39;t let billionaires buy themselves an exemption to paying taxes!</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R32" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>33</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-43-tax-threshold/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976472330&amp;usg=AOvVaw3C6wtiivt49sMV2ypF9zDJ">Prop 43 - Increase vote thresholds</a></td><td class="s1">❌❌❌</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Don&#39;t disenfranchise voters from funding public services that the majority of us want!</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R33" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>34</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-44-clinic-funding/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976472574&amp;usg=AOvVaw25-2hXOxaHu0qMANpHN8aB">Prop 44 - Clinic funding</a></td><td class="s1">❌</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Increases the cost of compliance without fixing the real problem of divestment in healthcare</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R34" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>35</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s3"><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-45-environmental-review/&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1793628976472889&amp;usg=AOvVaw18CbrTSiv4HloJIhTvcjOA">Prop 45 - More highways</a></td><td class="s1">❌❌❌</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Say no to industry passing their own custom law to unilaterally expand highways, suburbarn sprawl, and datacenters. It even bans streamlining HSR.</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R35" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>36</div></th><td class="s4"></td><td class="s1">Prop RTM - Regional Transit Funding</td><td class="s1">✅✅✅</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Save bay area transit! If this doesn&#39;t pass then it would result in a massive cut to service which would strand riders and drivers alike</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R36" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>37</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2"></td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R37" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>38</div></th><td class="s0" colspan="2">Transit</td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2"></td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R38" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>39</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1">AC Transit Ward 3</td><td class="s1">Adriana Valencia</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Valencia will work on service, reliability and transparency, and most importantly will kick Young off the board who actively works against riders</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R39" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>40</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1">AC Transit Ward 4</td><td class="s1">Sarah Syed</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Syed is a fierce advovate for riders and operators</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R40" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>41</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1">AC Transit Ward 5</td><td class="s1">Murphy McCulley</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">McCulley is the current Director and does a decent job</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R41" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>42</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1">BART D4</td><td class="s1">Robert Raburn</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Raburn is the current Director and is dedicated to improving transit for riders</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R42" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>43</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2"></td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R43" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>44</div></th><td class="s0" colspan="2">Oakland</td><td class="s1"></td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2"></td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R44" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>45</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1">Mayor</td><td class="s1">Barbara Lee</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Lee has been doing a decent job, and has no challenger from the left</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R45" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>46</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1">Auditor</td><td class="s1">Michael Houston</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Houston has been a good auditor. I have appreciated his educational public reports</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R46" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>47</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1">D2</td><td class="s1">Nate Adams</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Adams is DSA. Wang has been good on traffic safety, but vetoed homeless shelters and approved Flock despite the many known issues</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R47" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>48</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1">Measure EE</td><td class="s1">❌</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Council-Manager is more democratic and less corrupt. Strong mayor cities end up run more by donors than residents</td></tr><tr><th id="51332860R48" class="row-headers-background row-header-shim"><div>49</div></th><td class="s0"></td><td class="s1">Measure FF</td><td class="s1">✅</td><td class="s2"></td><td class="s2">Fix the foreclosure loophole that allows banks to bypass taxes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div><script nonce="viJ0GIwCjaQscm6hrOwhvw">switchToSheet('51332860');</script></body></html>